User: How do tariff rates affect terms of trade between trading partners?
Assistant: Tariffs affect terms of trade through several mechanisms depending on country size and market structure. For large countries, import tariffs can improve terms of trade by reducing world demand for imported goods, thereby lowering their relative prices. This terms-of-trade gain must be weighed against the deadweight loss from consumption and production distortions. The net welfare effect depends on the tariff level, with the optimal tariff balancing marginal terms-of-trade benefits against marginal efficiency costs. Small countries face perfectly elastic world supply curves and cannot affect world prices through tariffs. Empirical evidence suggests terms-of-trade effects are significant for large economies in concentrated industries but modest for most bilateral trade relationships.

